<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:25:35.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson--intro-web-page-844673ca-be59-4a9b-af6c-7fecd89418bb",
        "text": "Ever wonder how websites like this one are made? A web page is a document that can be displayed in a web browser, like Chrome or Safari.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/0cb73c0dc68e1df5c6af87e225e8f2f7-test-lesson--intro-web-page-panel-1-469dde5a-df07-4713-8b87-b4eb5497de42.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson--intro-web-page-cd2df291-af90-4475-8f9d-ef3c7117171f",
        "text": "Think of a web page like a house. HTML (HyperText Markup Language) provides the *structure* – the walls, doors, and rooms.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d89f0880f43c8033190c5cd86ad6a1be-test-lesson--intro-web-page-panel-2-1d92c61d-b84f-418c-a733-4fdf064e448d.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson--intro-web-page-69804602-494c-4065-bdf0-4ee086e49395",
        "text": "CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) adds the *style* – the paint colors, furniture, and landscaping that make it look good.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/183e59f9cfd9e6f83bc1c8209032ccd0-test-lesson--intro-web-page-panel-3-6e243ff7-aa50-4393-8485-f62a6aa6f5fd.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson--intro-web-page-a1f47682-5500-488c-978f-454b4bea33d0",
        "text": "Together, HTML and CSS create the complete, beautiful web pages you see every day. HTML gives it meaning, and CSS makes it shine!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/1e0196cd9bef43cd8e488f176db1a2be-test-lesson--intro-web-page-panel-4-9951d4d0-53e1-4b89-a2a9-5a446511ba61.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_outline": "Introduce students to the concept of a web page, explaining that it's made up of different parts like structure (HTML) and style (CSS). Use visuals to show how these components combine to create what they see in a browser."
  },
  "published": true,
